.\" Manual page for clishe, maintained in Sym-jay/clishe.
.TH CLISHE 1 "2026" "clishe 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
clishe \- describe what you want in plain English, and learn the command
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B clishe
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B clishe
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B clishe
.RI [ phrase ]
.br
.B clishe
.BI "explain " command
.br
.B clishe
.BI "check " command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B clishe
helps people who do not know the command line yet. Type what you want in plain
English, see the real command with each part labelled, and run it if you want to.
Nothing runs without your say-so.
.PP
It works offline: a bundled knowledge base, a command dictionary, your own
.BR man (1)
pages and the bundled tldr-pages data answer before any AI is asked. AI help is
optional, and by default it runs on your own machine. Cloud AI is never
enabled unless you ask for it.
.PP
Run
.B clishe
with no arguments to start an interactive session.
.SH ONE-SHOT COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "explain " command
Explain what a command does, flag by flag, then exit.
.TP
.I practice " [lesson]"
Hands-on exercises in a throwaway folder.
.B clishe practice --list
shows the bundled lessons.
.TP
.B progress
The everyday commands you have learned to type yourself.
.TP
.B setup
Find or set up a local AI model.
.TP
.B tour
A quick tour of your own computer: system, disk, folders, installing software.
.TP
.B doctor
Check the setup, and how to fix anything wrong.
.TP
.B sheet
Your own cheat sheet of the commands you have learned. Save it with
.BR "clishe sheet > cheatsheet.txt" .
.TP
.BI "check " command
Say what a command or script would do, without running it. Exits 1 when there
are warnings, so it works in scripts.
.TP
.B "phrase"
Look up a phrase in the knowledge base and print the command. It does not run
it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the built-in help.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Show the version.
.TP
.B \-\-list
Show the phrases you have taught Clishe.
.TP
.BI "\-\-init " "bash|zsh"
Print the Ctrl+G shortcut (and Tab completion) for your normal shell. Add the
printed line to your startup file:
.B eval "$(clishe --init bash)"
for bash, or
.B eval "$(clishe --init zsh)"
for zsh.
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Words instead of symbols and drawings, for screen readers. The same thing can
be set permanently with
.B "plain": true
in the config file.
.SH SESSION COMMANDS
Inside a session you can type plain English or a normal shell command. These
words do something else:
.TP
.B help
Show tips.
.TP
.B learned
List the phrases you have taught.
.TP
.B teach
Teach a phrase and its command, or fix a wrong one.
.TP
.BI "forget " phrase
Forget a phrase you taught.
.TP
.B practice " [lesson]"
Hands-on exercises in a throwaway folder.
.TP
.B progress
What you have learned, and what to learn next.
.TP
.B setup
Find or set up a local AI model.
.TP
.B tour
A quick tour of your own computer.
.TP
.B doctor
Check the setup.
.TP
.B sheet
Your own cheat sheet.
.TP
.BI "explain " command
Explain a command and its flags.
.TP
.B what does this mean
Explain the output of the command you just ran.
.TP
.B fix that
Explain why the last command failed, and offer a fix.
.TP
.B undo that
Reverse the last change, showing the command first.
.TP
.BI "check " command
Is it safe? What would it change?
.TP
.B exit
Leave. Ctrl-D works too.
.PP
Commands with
.IR <placeholders> ,
like
.BR "cp <file> <destination>" ,
ask you to fill in each value before anything runs.
.SH SAFETY
Commands that look destructive need you to type
.B YES
before they run, and the warning says why in plain English
("It deletes a folder and everything inside it, permanently"). The check parses
the command, so
.BR "rm -fr" ,
.BR "sudo rm -r" ,
.BR "cd x && rm -rf y" ,
.B "curl ... | sh"
and
.B "git reset --hard"
are all caught.
.PP
When you delete something with
.BR rm ,
Clishe offers to move it to the Trash instead, if
.B gio
or
.B trash-cli
is installed, so you can get it back.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/clishe/config.json
Settings: AI providers, plain mode, learning mode. See
.B clishe doctor .
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/clishe/
Your knowledge base, your history and your own cheat sheet.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/clishe/lessons/
Put your own practice lessons here, as JSON, and run
.BR "clishe practice <name>" .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CLISHE_DEBUG
Let Python errors show instead of being hidden. Useful when something does
nothing.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Turn off colour.
.SH AI PROVIDERS
By default Clishe only talks to an AI running on your own machine: Ollama, or
any server with an OpenAI-style API (llama.cpp, LM Studio, Jan, LocalAI,
vLLM). It finds a running server by itself. A server on the internet is refused
unless you set
.B "allow_remote_ai": true
in the config.
.PP
Anthropic is available as an opt-in and does nothing until you set
.B "enabled": true
in its block in the config.
.SH NOTES
Works on Linux and macOS. On Windows, use WSL.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B clishe explain 'tar -xzvf'
Explain the flags of an archive command.
.TP
.B clishe 'show me disk usage'
Print the command for a phrase, without running it.
.TP
.B clishe check 'curl example.com/install.sh | sudo bash'
Say what it would do, and flag the risky parts.
.TP
.B eval "$(clishe --init zsh)"
Use plain English at your normal prompt: type it, press Ctrl+G, read the
command, then press Enter when you are ready.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR man (1),
.BR bash (1),
.BR zsh (1)
.PP
